{"_id":"68dcfaea166b018f83df7b6b","roadmapSlug":"css","nodeId":"ZyqKZMIkQ22ysFqmhL3ZN","description":"# Direction\n\nThe `direction` property in CSS sets the text direction of block-level elements, influencing how text, table columns, and inline-level boxes flow. While `direction` can be used to switch between left-to-right (LTR) and right-to-left (RTL) layouts, it's generally better to use the HTML `dir` global attribute. The `dir` attribute semantically indicates the document's or element's text direction, providing better accessibility and separation of concerns compared to styling direction with CSS.","resources":[{"type":"article","title":"CSS Direction","url":"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/direction","_id":"6a67293033d15c8310214482"},{"type":"article","title":"HTML dir global attribute","url":"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTML/Reference/Global_attributes/dir","_id":"6a67293033d15c8310214483"},{"type":"video","title":"CSS for beginners 60: direction property","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=LM0yIWmP62Q","_id":"6a67293033d15c8310214484"},{"type":"video","title":"HTML Global Attributes - dir Attribute","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=6hqHM7Ez_Xg","_id":"6a67293033d15c8310214485"}],"createdAt":"2025-10-01T09:56:58.848Z","updatedAt":"2026-07-27T09:47:28.129Z","lessonPacks":[{"_id":"6a22adddac1c5fa9928ab3ab","title":"CSS Fundamentals","slug":"css","description":"Style, lay out, and debug real pages without fighting the cascade.","lessonIds":["6a15d62fac1c5fa9928a3fb6","6a15e1b0ac1c5fa9928a403f","6a16f11aac1c5fa9928a7c14","6a19dcdfac1c5fa9928a84a5","6a19e79cac1c5fa9928a8571","6a19f85cac1c5fa9928a8654","6a1d7a23ac1c5fa9928a8b4e","6a1dd2daac1c5fa9928a9884","6a1ecf18ac1c5fa9928a9a81","6a1f3245ac1c5fa9928a9cdd","6a20aa64ac1c5fa9928aa44a","6a20ba69ac1c5fa9928aa755","6a20c105ac1c5fa9928aa818","6a20c2e5ac1c5fa9928aa847","6a20c490ac1c5fa9928aa871","6a20c5adac1c5fa9928aa884","6a20c6a5ac1c5fa9928aa897","6a20c7c5ac1c5fa9928aa8aa"